{
  "version": 1,
  "created": "2026-08-06",
  "owner": "founder-directed 2026-08-06; codes are internal identity, never a provider's",
  "why": [
    "The 22 cultural DOMAINS in worker/importers/domain_map.py are ratified and are LAYER 1 here, unchanged and re-exported, so nothing forks.",
    "LAYER 2 (subsegment) exists today ONLY as a passthrough of Ticketmaster/SeatGeek genre strings. That means a crawled venue event can never receive one, and our sub-taxonomy is owned by a vendor. This file makes layer 2 ours.",
    "LAYER 3 (sub-subsegment) does not exist anywhere in the tree. It is the level at which a person actually chooses a night out: not 'live-music' but 'singer-songwriter residency'.",
    "Codes are STABLE and opaque so an entity can be tagged once and re-labelled later without rewriting rows. Labels are display text and may change; codes may not."
  ],
  "code_rules": {
    "segment": "2-3 uppercase letters, unique",
    "subsegment": "<SEGMENT>-<3 letters>",
    "sub_subsegment": "<SUBSEGMENT>-<3 letters>",
    "assignment": "An entity carries the DEEPEST code that is EVIDENCED. Partial is normal and honest: LM is a complete answer when the act is unknown. Never deepen a code by inference — an unevidenced sub-subsegment is worse than an absent one."
  },
